  "question": "What does the Latin legend on the Oc Eo gold medallion read?",
  "answer": "The Latin legend on the Óc Eo gold medallion is recorded as \"ANTONINVS AVG PIVS NVRP (or NVAP) XV,\" with the source noting this is a \"slightly corrupted Latin legend\" [S1]. The piece is a gold sheet imitating a Roman coin, 19mm in diameter, 0.3mm thick, weighing 1.4135g, with a fineness of 916 (22 carat) [S1]. It was formerly held in the Musee Blanchard de la Brosse, Saigon, under inventory number MBB 3460, and has been unlocated since 1975 [S1]. More broadly, the finds at Óc Eo include gold jewellery imitating Roman coins from the Antonine period, of which this medallion is an example [S2].",
